      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "عَلِيُّ بْنُ إِبْرَاهِيمَ عَنْ أَبِيهِ وَ مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ يَحْيَى عَنْ أَحْمَدَ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ جَمِيعاً عَنِ ابْنِ أَبِي عُمَيْرٍ عَنْ حَمَّادِ بْنِ عُثْمَانَ عَنِ الْحَلَبِيِّ عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) أَنَّهُ سُئِلَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Ali ibn Ibrahim, from his father, and Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Ahmad ibn Muhammad, all from Ibn Abi Umayr, from Hammad ibn Uthman, from Al-Halabi, from Abu Abdillah (peace be upon him), that he was asked"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "عَنْ رَجُلٍ نَسِيَ فَأَكَلَ وَ شَرِبَ ثُمَّ ذَكَرَ قَالَ لَا يُفْطِرْ إِنَّمَا هُوَ شَيْ‏ءٌ رَزَقَهُ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ فَلْيُتِمَّ صَوْمَهُ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "about a man who forgot, so he ate and drank, then remembered. He (peace be upon him) said: 'He should not break the fast. It is merely something Allah, Mighty and Majestic, granted him, so let him complete his fast.'"
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "This hadith establishes the legal ruling for a person who eats or drinks during Ramadan out of forgetfulness. The Imam (peace be upon him) rules that their fast remains valid and they do not need to make up for it, as the eating/drinking is considered a grace from Allah.",
      "seo_question": "Does eating or drinking out of forgetfulness break the fast in Ramadan?",
      "key_terms": {
        "نَسِيَ": "forgot",
        "يُفْطِرْ": "break the fast",
        "صَوْمَهُ": "his fast",
        "رَزَقَهُ": "He granted him"
      }
    }
  },
